    "created_at": "2023-02-27T21:13:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-02-27T21:13:01Z",
    "body": "I don't know why I thought it was working, it wasn't. I decided to take a completely different approach, and changed my prompt to use the backspace character instead of the fancy new zero width space. \r\n\r\nIt seems to work, and I would expect it to be more compatible with various shells and terminals, so maybe it would make sense for the built-in pure theme to use it?\r\n```toml\r\nconflicted = \" \\b\"\r\nuntracked = \" \\b\"\r\nmodified = \" \\b\"\r\nstaged = \" \\b\"\r\nrenamed = \" \\b\"\r\ndeleted = \" \\b\"\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
