    "created_at": "2023-03-27T14:43:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-27T15:29:00Z",
    "body": "This issue is also related to these feature requests\r\n- https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/4387\r\n- https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/1192\r\n\r\nPut simply, if there were a `dirty` property on the `git_status` configuration, we wouldn't have to do all these gymnastics in the Pure preset: `[(*$conflicted$untracked$modified$staged$renamed$deleted)]($style)\"`\r\n\r\nAnd, heaven help you if you ever try to use the `u200b` zero-width space trickery to put your git_status on a right prompt - the issues are even more profound.\r\n\r\nIn the meantime, [using this custom command](https://github.com/starship/starship/discussions/1252#discussioncomment-692829) seems to do the trick. This should be the new Pure-Preset.toml file:\r\n\r\n```toml\r\nformat = \"\"\"\r\n$username\\\r\n$hostname\\\r\n$directory\\\r\n$git_branch\\\r\n$git_state\\\r\n${custom.git_status_dirty}\\\r\n$git_status\\\r\n$cmd_duration\\\r\n$line_break\\\r\n$python\\\r\n$character\"\"\"\r\n\r\n[directory]\r\nstyle = \"blue\"\r\n\r\n[character]\r\nsuccess_symbol = \"[❯](purple)\"\r\nerror_symbol = \"[❯](red)\"\r\nvicmd_symbol = \"[❮](green)\"\r\n\r\n[git_branch]\r\nformat = \"[$branch]($style)\"\r\nstyle = \"bright-black\"\r\n\r\n[git_status]\r\nformat = \"[($ahead_behind$stashed)]($style)\"\r\nstyle = \"cyan\"\r\nstashed = \"≡\"\r\n\r\n[custom.git_status_dirty]\r\nwhen = 'test -n \"$(git status --porcelain)\"'\r\nsymbol = \"*\"\r\nstyle = \"purple\"\r\nformat=\"[$symbol]($style) \"\r\nshell = [\"bash\", \"--norc\", \"--noprofile\"]\r\n\r\n[git_state]\r\nformat = '\\([$state( $progress_current/$progress_total)]($style)\\) '\r\nstyle = \"bright-black\"\r\n\r\n[cmd_duration]\r\nformat = \"[$duration]($style) \"\r\nstyle = \"yellow\"\r\n\r\n[python]\r\nformat = \"[$virtualenv]($style) \"\r\nstyle = \"bright-black\"\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
